1027: a second swap slot (kern.bergamota_fb_queue2, default off). (Brightness_Scale, first added here, is patch 1029.)

With async commits (1022) a swap arriving while another is pending held CoreAnimation's display thread in SwapEnd (1023)
until the vsync tick took the pending one; that wait ended just after the next tick, which CoreAnimation then missed:
frames whose encode + GPU work take longer than one refresh were shown every other refresh (30 fps). With the sysctl
set, the second swap waits in a second slot, promoted when the pending one is taken. Applies after 1026.

Diagnostics: kern.bergamota_fb gains queued= (swaps put in the second slot) and held_reuse= (swaps onto a surface a pending or
queued swap still shows: the stale-frame case).
Ordering: a swap that goes straight to pending (the slot was empty for a moment during the early path's zero-copy try, or the
display was off) drops an older queued swap, and promotion only moves forward in swap id (both counted: next_dropped).
order_back= counts frames taken older than the one before them. Without this a queued frame was shown after a newer one: stale frames.

